ng turn and come across an abandoned amusement park. When her parents get into a trouble, Chihiro finds they are trapped in a world of spirits, gods and monsters. She soon finds herself on a magical journey, where she discovers a world beyond her imagination!\n\nHayao Miyazaki is an animated film director. Born 1941, Tokyo. After graduating from Gakushuin University in 1963 with a degree in Political Science and Economics, Hayao Miyazaki joined Toei Animation as an animator. Miyazaki co-founded Studio Ghibli in 1985 with Takahata. Representative works include Nausicaä of the Valley of the Wind (1984), Castle in the Sky (1986), My Neighbor Totoro (1988), Princess Mononoke (1997), Spirited Away (2001), Howl’s Moving Castle (2004), Ponyo (2008), and The Wind Rises (2013), among others. His latest film is The Boy and the Heron (2023).\nSpirited Away broke every box office record in Japan, and garnered many awards, including the Golden Bear at the 2002 Berlin International Film Festival and the 2002 Academy Award® for Best Animated Feature Film. Miyazaki was awarded the Golden Lion for Lifetime Achievement at the 2005 Venice International Film Festival. In 2012, Miyazaki was named a “Person of Cultural Merit” by the government of Japan. In November 2014, the Board of Governors for the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences presented him with an Honorary Oscar® for Lifetime Achievement.\nAdditionally, he was responsible for the original concept, planning, and production of the Ghibli Museum, which opened in Mitaka in 2001, for which he serves as Honorary Executive Director.\n\n#### Spirited Away Film Comic: All-in-One Edition\n\nChihiro’s family is moving to a new house, but when they stop on the way to explore an abandoned village, her parents undergo a mysterious transformation and Chihiro is whisked into a world of fantastic spirits ruled over by the sorceress Yubaba. Put to work in a magical bath house for spirits and demons, Chihiro must use all her wits to survive in this strange new place, find a way to free her parents and return to the normal world.\nExperience one of Hayao Miyazaki’s most critically acclaimed animated films in a deluxe hardcover volume!\n\nBuy now\n\n### Other Spirited Away volumes\n\nSee all >\n\n+26\n\nPicture Book\n\nSpirited Away Picture Book\n\n+79\n\nArt Book\n\nThe Art of Spirited Away\n\n+42\n\nFilm Comic\n\nSpirited Away Film Comic, Vol. 5\n\n+31\n\nFilm Comic\n\nSpirited Away Film Comic, Vol. 4\n\nSee all >--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVIZ | Copyrights (https://www.viz.com/copyrights)\nciteturn33search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Frankenstein: Junji Ito Story Collection  |    | © JI Inc. ... Spirited Away, The Art of  |    | Spirited Away (Sen to Chihiro no Kamikakushi)\n \n \nSpirited Away Picture Book  |    | Spirited Away (Sen to Chihiro no Kamikakushi)\n© 2001 Hayao Miyazaki/Studio Ghibli, NDDTM\n \n \nSpirited Away, The Art of  |    | Spirited Away (Sen to Chihiro no Kamikakushi)\n© 2001 Hayao Miyazaki/Studio Ghibli, NDDTM\n \n \nSpirit Photographer Saburo Kono  |    | SHINREI SHASHINSHI KONO SABURO © 2020 by Kaiu Shirai, Posuka Demizu/SHUEISHA Inc.\n \n \nSplatoon  |    | TM& © 2017 Nintendo\nSPLATOON © 2016 Sankichi HINODEYA/SHOGAKUKAN\n \n \nSplatoon: Squid Kids Comedy Show  |    | TM & © 2020 Nintendo\nSPLATOON IKASU KIDS 4KOMA FES © 2018 Hideki GOTO/SHOGAKUKAN\n \n \nSporting Salt  |    | SPORTING SALT © 2014 by Yuto Kubota/SHUEISHA Inc.\n \n \nSpring Weapon No. 01  |    | SPRING WEAPON No. 01 © 2016 by Tomohiro Hasegawa/SHUEISHA Inc.\n \n \nStarting Point 1979~1996  |    | © 1996 Studio Ghibli\n \nStatues: Junji Ito Story Collection  |    | © JI Inc./Asahi Shimbun Publications Inc.\n \n \n \nStatus Royale  |    | © Ru Xu\n \n \n \nStar Brighter than the Sun, A  |    | TAIYO YORIMO MABUSHII HOSHI © 2021 by Kazune Kawahara/SHUEISHA Inc.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVIZ | 